I can't tell what these features are: the names are anonymized, and I have no data or descriptions to go on. The Adult census dataset has 14 raw attributes, and 63 columns suggests a one-hot encoded version, but the column order is unknown. Any ordering I assumed would be a guess.

One common layout is age, fnlwgt, education-num, capital-gain, capital-loss and hours-per-week as the numeric columns, followed by one-hot columns for the categorical attributes. Another is a mix in the original order. Without confirmation, I'm giving every feature the same low-moderate score, with slightly higher values for the early indices, which are more likely to be numeric features such as age and education-num.


